+## Amended in session 15c
+
+**A proposal never ends unanswered without an ending.**
+
+- A new ask over an open proposal ends it `stopped`, the ending a stop mid-plan already writes: the user replaced it, and the new run follows it in the same negotiation.
+- An open adaptation whose day is reported ends `overtaken`, the seventh ending: the engine would refuse to prescribe it (`mesocycles.still_today`), and nothing follows it.
+- Either is written by resuming the proposal with `planner.unanswered(ending)`, so the graph writes it like any other.
+- A run the entrance carries into a subgraph is on both their threads; the reader counts it once, as the subgraph's.
+
 ## Consequences
 
 - **`record.Run` goes.** The model, provider and budget carried in the run's config were the identity of a run answered by one model; the model belongs to the node that did the work and goes in the record's node entries.
